            <ArticleTitle>The hourglass sign.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00261-017-1321-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Hourglass sign is a useful imaging clue for diagnosing diaphragmatic ruptures with viscera herniation on multidetector CT, with a sensitivity ranging from 16% to 63% and a specificity around 98%-100%. This sign is also commonly found in the literature under the name &quot;Collar sign,&quot; first described in 1995 by Worthy et al. It refers to the waistlike constriction of the herniated structure at the site of the diaphragmatic rupture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
